  "refuter_findings": [
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:15:1",
      "id": "ex-product-foliation",
      "location": "Example",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The claim is that \"the sets M x {q} for q in N form a regular foliation.\" No connectedness of M is assumed. Take M to be a discrete two-point smooth 0-manifold. Then M x {q} has two connected components, while the repository's definition of a leaf requires a maximal connected subset; the zero-dimensional product foliation has the two singleton components as leaves, not M x {q}. The claim needs M connected or must say connected components of the fibres.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "cb27b2d089098ab63bad88f3333b379609c1e3f891fad7adf25190bd4d3c06aa"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:15:2",
      "id": "ex-the-mobius-band-line-foliation",
      "location": "Example",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The Example says that every leaf with t != 0 \"is a copy of R winding once around the band before returning with the opposite transverse sign.\" In the stated quotient, following the horizontal direction from [(0,t)] to [(1,t)] reaches [(0,-t)]; following it once more reaches [(0,t)]. Thus the horizontal integral curve through t != 0 is periodic with two traversals and its leaf is a circle, not a copy of R.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "1128909d5f37395a3b6c9e71c58e43a3a26d22a2c6d5ab17c17f16e21a467973"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:15:3",
      "id": "lem-involutive-frame-reduction",
      "location": "Proof 1.3",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 1.2 defines [X_1,Z_j] = sum_l c_{j l} Z_l and solves partial_t B = -C B, while step 1.3 sets Y_j = sum_l B_{l j}Z_l. The coefficient of Z_r in [X_1,Y_j] is partial_t B_{rj} + sum_l B_{l j}c_{l r}, namely (B' + C^T B)_{rj}; the stated ODE instead gives B' + C B = 0. These do not agree generally. For D = T R^3 with X_1 = partial_t, Z_2 = partial_u, and Z_3 = t partial_u + partial_v, one has c_{32}=1. The prescribed ODE gives Y_2 = Z_2 - t Z_3, but [X_1,Y_2] = -Z_3 - t Z_2 != 0. Thus the claimed commuting frame does not follow.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "bf83a73956af41e6f1c1d77bfe4e3e344a20d15270471c916c2f0db1c6fb5895"
    }
  ],
